[580.606, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[4B\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mtile_into\u001b[39m takes 0.76 \u001b[26Go\u001b[29Gth\u001b[32G real w\u001b[40Gights, versus about 0.15 s predicted, because the machine is short\u001b[107Gon memory\u001b[117Gwith\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bheavy compression.\u001b[22GI'm comparing old and n\u001b[46Gw loading\u001b[56Gback to\u001b[64Gb\u001b[66Gck\u001b[69Gnext.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[4BLoading takes about the same time\u001b[37Gin both version\u001b[53G within one process, so\u001b[77Gthe extra cost comes from first-touch\u001b[115Gpage\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfaults in fresh processes under memory pressure. I'm now comparing the two versions \u001b[88Gn fresh process\u001b[104Gs, and\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmemory-m\u001b[12Gpping the ch\u001b[25Gckpo\u001b[30Gnt is\u001b[36Ga\u001b[38Gway\u001b[42Gto\u001b[45Gavoid\u001b[51Gthe\u001b[55G438\u001b[59GMB\u001b[62Gof\u001b[65Gfresh\u001b[71Ganonymous\u001b[81Gmemory.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[4Bmemmap source wins in fresh processes (about 0.40 s versus 0.48\u20130.80 s),\u001b[80Gso I'm switching to it\u001b[104Gnd us\u001b[110Gng\u001b[113Gthe\u001b[117G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfa\u001b[6Gte\u001b[9G branch-fre\u001b[21G 16\u00d716 copy\u001b[33Gfor full tiles, with a gen\u001b[60Gric path for any\u001b[77Gpa\u001b[80Gded tail.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shel"]
