[741.046, "\u001b]0;\u25d1 Claude Code\u0007"]
[741.054, "\u001b[H\u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m05\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mbytes (quantization) or more core\u001b[48G, and the rules forbid b\u001b[73Gth.\u001b[77GFurther tuning attempts (ti\u001b[105Ge   \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m06\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mwidth, unroll dept\u001b[33G) were\u001b[40Gwithin noise.         \u001b[63G   \u001b[67G     \u001b[73G    \u001b[78G  \u001b[81G \u001b[83G     \u001b[89G       \u001b[97G     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 207 \u001b[22m - **Summation order**: each matvec output is summed in the same order as run.c. Numba emits no\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  76 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  FMA \u001b[48;2;255;199;199mhere \u001b[48;2;255;220;220m(no `contract` flag), while the build that produced the fixtures may have fused            \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m08\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mFMA (no `contract` flag)\u001b[40Gwhile th\u001b[49G build\u001b[56Gthat produced the fixtures\u001b[83Gm\u001b[85Gy\u001b[87Ghave\u001b[92Gfused    \u001b[102G  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 209 \u001b[22m   multiply-adds. The differences are ~1e-5 in the logits.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  "]
[741.056, "78 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Load-time transpose**: weights sit in memory once, in transposed form, plus an extra 98 MB        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m  79 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  transposed classifier copy because the classifier is shared with the embedding. Peak memory         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;207;34;46m  80 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  during load is about 1 GB.                                                                          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m 210 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Memory**: the tiled weights (438 MB) and the tiled classifier copy (98 MB, because it is          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 211 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  shared with the 98 MB embedding) stay resident. The checkpoint is mapped read-only during load.     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 212 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  Load time depends heavily on OS memory pressure: the first load in a fresh process after            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 213 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  recompiling or under pressure was seen at up to ~1.6 s.                            "]
[741.058, "                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 214 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Long contexts**: attention and the KV-cache stores grow with position. They are 3% at the dev     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 215 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  workloads' \u226482 positions, but larger near seq_len = 1024. That range was only exercised by          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 216 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  `edge.py` (~10.8 s for 1016 forced + 9 new positions), not profiled in detail.                      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 217 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Startup** (~1.3\u20131.6 s): ~0.55 s is importing numpy+numba, ~0.4 s is loading and tiling, and       \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m18\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \u001b[14G~0.1 \u001b[20G is a warm-up forward. T\u001b[45Ger\u001b[49Gis no further easy cut within the \u001b[84Gules.   \u001b[93G         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 219 \u001b[22m - **Numba on-disk cache** (`cache=True`) writes compiled code to `__pycache__/` beside `run.py`.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 220 \u001b[22m   Without it (e.g. a read-only dir with no fallback), the first star"]
[741.059, "t compiles for a few seconds.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 221 \u001b[22m   Before `READY`, a single warm-up forward runs and the KV cache is reset afterwards.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m...\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 226 \u001b[22m   not range-checked (bounds checks are off in the kernels).\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 227 \u001b[22m - The tokenizer and protocol handling are plain Python (not compute); only the arithmetic is\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B    \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 228 \u001b[22m   compiled.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m    \u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  91 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- Throughput on this machine moved a lot between runs (roughly 62\u2013104 tok/s for the same command),    \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m    \u001b[38;2;207;34;46m\u001b[48;2;255;220;220m  92 -\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  apparently from other load, so the speed figures above are rough.                                   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m 229 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Measurement noise**: the machine was shared and memory-pressured throug"]
[741.06, "hout. Identical            \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[4G  \u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m 230 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m  commands varied by \u00b115\u201330% between runs, so treat the figures as medians under that load.           \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m \u001b[39m Running \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ rm -rf scratch/__pycache__ && python3 check.py --tokens 64 --prompts 3 -- python3 run.py | tail -1 && ls scratch\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2733\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;245;149;117mFluttering\u2026\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m(11m 57s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[28G53.7k tokens)\r\u001b[1B  \u23bf \u00a0Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B      \u001b[14G        \u001b[23G  \u001b[26G                      \u001b[103G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u25cf high \u00b7 /effort\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;138;138;138m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500"]
[741.061, "\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f\u00a0\u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;138;138;138m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23f8 manual mode on \u00b7\u001b[22Gesc to interrupt\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
